{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 4, :comments ["<b>Of the seed of Aaron.</b> It was necessary to mention them a second time, to say that they specifically require the setting of the sun [for their purification], but consecrated foods that Israelites eat — which are [second tithe] — do not require the setting of the sun. Thus they expounded in Torat Kohanim." "And the verse says <b>and he is afflicted with tzara'at</b>, they expounded in Torat Kohanim, and this is their language: I have only his seed; from where do I derive himself? Scripture teaches by saying ״וְהוּא״ — and so forth. End quote. Now, regarding this reasoning, it is impossible to say what we explained concerning the verse (Leviticus 21:7) ״אִישׁ מִזַּרְעֲךָ״, for — HaShem preserve us — since here there is also ״אֲשֶׁר תֵּצֵא מִמֶּנּוּ שִׁכְבַת זָרַע״, and we find that Aaron did not separate from his wife; and if it had not said ״וְהוּא״, there would have been room to say that Aaron may eat consecrated foods in a state of impurity — Scripture therefore teaches ״וְהוּא״. And since Aaron was included, his sons were also included. From now on, [consider] the first verse, which said ״אִישׁ מִזַּרְעֲךָ אֲשֶׁר יִהְיֶה בוֹ מוּם״ and Aaron was not included — say from now on that he is not included, and the reason is that he is assured that HaShem will guard him and his sons lest a blemish befall them, as I have written."], :book :leviticus, :voice :or-hachaim, :lang :en, :chapter 22, :notes {1 "The bracketed correction from הַשְּׁלָמִים (peace-offerings) to מַעֲשֵׂר שֵׁנִי (second tithe) is printed in the source text; I have translated the corrected reading."}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T20:00:19.066606923Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}